  'site.calculators.rentVsBuy.tableNote': 'Net property equity = property value − remaining loan − selling cost, at the end of each year. The highlighted row is the estimated break-even year.',
  'site.calculators.rentVsBuy.method': 'How it is calculated: Net Buy Cost = total buy outflows (down payment + stamp duty + registration + purchase costs + EMIs paid in the 120 months + maintenance) − net sale equity (property value after 10 years − remaining loan − selling cost) + opportunity cost (down payment × (1 + return)¹⁰ − down payment). Net Rent Cost = total rent paid, with rent rising once a year. EMI = P × r × (1 + r)ⁿ ÷ ((1 + r)ⁿ − 1), the same formula as the Home Loan calculator; the loan is not treated as paid off after 10 years. Break-even is the first year from which buying stays lower-cost through year 10.',
  'site.calculators.rentVsBuy.excluded': 'Not included in this version: property tax, home insurance, GST and other taxes, income-tax benefits on home loans, investing any monthly difference between EMI + maintenance and rent, and the opportunity cost of stamp duty, registration and purchase costs. Property tax is not included in this version. Home insurance is not included in this version.',
